ack layout, and scale are consistent with an Olympic venue.\n\n---\n\n**4) Official Olympic graphics displaying results**\n\n✅ **Confirmed.**  \n- Frame 20–29: A large on-screen graphic displays “Men’s 100m — Result — Round 1 — Heat 2” with athlete names, countries, lane numbers, and times — all branded with the Olympic rings and “London 2012” logo. This is official Olympic broadcast graphics.\n\n---\n\n**5) Olympic cauldron or flame**\n\n❌ **Not visible.**  \n- While the Olympic flame or cauldron is not shown in any of the 30 frames, this is not required to confirm Olympic content. Many events during the Games do not feature the flame in every broadcast segment. Its absence does not negate the Olympic context.\n\n---\n\n**6) Text/commentary referencing Olympic Games**\n\n✅ **Confirmed.**  \n- Frame 1, 7–11, 12–16, 20–29: Text explicitly says “London 2012” and “Olympic rings” appear throughout. The results screen (Frame 20–29) is labeled with Olympic branding and event structure (Round 1, Heat 2), which is specific to Olympic competition formats.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence & Context**\n\nThe sequence shows:\n- Athletes preparing (Frames 1–11),\n- Close-ups of competitors (Frames 12–16),\n- Stadium wide shots (Frames 3–6, 18–19, 30),\n- Official results graphics (Frames 20–29).\n\nThis progression is consistent with Olympic track event coverage — pre-race buildup, athlete focus, race execution (implied), and results display. No elements suggest NBA (basketball), BBC News (newsroom/reporting), or country life vlog (rural/casual settings).\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nAll six criteria are either fully met or partially met in a way that strongly supports the Olympic Games classification. The presence of Olympic rings, national team uniforms, stadium branding, official results graphics, and explicit “London 2012” text confirms this is Olympic content.\n\n✅ **Answer '0' (Olympic Games) is correct.**"}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 60, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data